  "notes": "# P0-41 bounded qualification \u2014 15 October 2026\n\nThe latest corrected private corpus passed 27 of 27 cases on measured source 33a8e20bf340f2f9c717bb813f95de3b648a4ad4. These are 12 supplied-input and 15 genuine local Git/CLI cases, not adopted permanent regression coverage or current program measurements. No tracked source or test was changed.\n\nThirteen original commands passed. The two private controls measured 27\u219219\u219227 and 27\u219226\u219227. Their six phases repeat the same 27 cases: 162 executions, 153 passes and nine body assertion failures across eight distinct names. Later assertions can be masked. The primary receipt records only the latest 27 passes; its 20 command rows retain the 13 original commands, six causal phases and one separately failed v1 baseline.\n\nThe v1 attempt remains 27 total, 26 passed and one fixture error: Git returned 1 where Q12d incorrectly demanded 128. Its following product refusal was masked; no mutant or restoration ran there. Only that Git precondition changed in a fresh v2 namespace, retaining the exact product refusal. Restored samples preserve actual missing-SHA refusal, genuine-ancestor structural acceptance, committed JSON zero despite working-copy changes/deletion, and Markdown escaping. They do not authenticate declarations or approved merges.\n\nThe empty-assertion control is a supplied-report unit computation. No successful CLI --vitest-json case, online cadence query, real owner measurement, full suite, coverage, Node 24, hosted CI or formal acceptance is claimed. All 15 current metric rows, 90 target cells, funded selection and unspecified A4 targets remain. Monday posting remains Sid's task. Required quality debt remains 1269 duplicate and 2751 dead-code findings, without waiver. P0-29's skipped unresolved routes and P0-22's successful empty passport-array contract remain unrelated and unresolved.\n\nThe WIP snapshot records 13 unreviewed bot PRs with no documented exemption; conservative new-admission hold remains. P0-57 is not activated: P1-65 freeze-exception and accepted-base barriers remain. All prior user holds, ownership, expert/ISO, release and source-transfer gaps remain. Review and root outcome retain detailed limits. Large manifests and both full runtime indices remain unsplit private references. This packet is qualification evidence, not Done, dependency closure or permission to publish.\n\nEvidence: [Bounded results](evidence/004-p0-41-bounded-qualification-20261015.json) \u00b7 [Actual evidence review](evidence/003-p0-41-bounded-independent-actual-review-20261015.md) \u00b7 [Root outcome and next-item holds](evidence/149-p0-41-root-outcome-20261015.json) \u00b7 [Receipt](receipt.json).\n\nThe staged whitespace check exited 2 for one blank line at the end of the original build log. Its bytes are preserved; [validation details](validation/augmentation.json) record the warning and passing receipt/freeze checks.\n"
